 pox in a man  who had recent contact with someone who  traveled to montreal this comes after  three more cases were confirmed in  quebec bringing the total in that  province to five the public health  agency of canada says it is still  investigating about two dozen other  suspected cases of the rare disease  earlier on friday chief public health  officer dr teresa tam said it's unclear  how widespread the disease has become in  this country  but stressed the risk to the public is  low  a common childhood virus called  adenovirus is now the leading hypothesis  for recent cases of severe hepatitis in  children that have led to at least six  deaths in the u.s  the cdc says it is investigating whether  180 cases identified since last october  represent an actual increase or whether  an existing pattern has been found  through improved detection  around half of the children diagnosed  recently also had adenovirus which  causes the common cold but the exact  cause of the illness is still under  investigation  there have also been 10 cases recorded  in canada  ahead on global national meal kits can  save food waste but are they saving you  any money  a state of local emergency was declared  in manitoba's white shell provincial  park last night as officials say rising  water levels posed a significant threat  to public safety the batula lake area  near the ontario border has been  evacuated with residents in the  surrounding areas being told to be ready  to leave at a moment's notice  well food inflation is at its worst in  four decades with prices up nearly 10  percent in the past year that has  prompted some households to turn to meal  kits as a way to manage costs and reduce  waste but azan gaviola explains in the  second story of our sticker shock series  it won't save you money  take this couple of peppers toronto  resident janie gandhi cooks at home a  lot but she finds the amount spent to  feed her family of four including two  active children shocking i just feel  terribly sad saying the numbers but it's  around 400 to 500 a week when it comes  to groceries every other week or so they  opt for meal kits it costs more but the  time saved is valuable they definitely  come in from the point of view of saving  time because it takes the whole pain out  of the whole cooking process of what's  the ingredient that i need how much  quantity i need and what am i cooking  today according to research by dalhousie  university people flocked to meal kits  at the start of the pandemic causing  canadian sales to peak at 1.6 million  dollars in the first six months but the  easing of covid restrictions and the  amount of packaging that comes with most  meal kit services plus sticker shock  have given many households food for  thought food inflation is probably the  biggest issue affecting households right  now  and that meal cuts tend to be priced  quite high eight to thirteen dollars on  average per meal per person global news  averaged out the cost per serving of  three leading meal kit companies a  family of four can expect to pay about  ten dollars per serving the cost per  serving for a household of two though  nearly twelve dollars inflation is  expected to push up the total food spend  for a typical family of four to more  than fourteen thousand seven hundred and  sixty dollars this year that's an  increase of nearly a thousand dollars  from twenty twenty one personal finance  expert rubina ahmed hawk says shopping  with a list can save you more than  twenty percent  before you leave make a plan of what  you're going to buy according to what's  on sale and buy only what you need with  smaller frequent trips  for this household meal kits are also a  new culinary adventure they're willing  to pay a premium for once in a while  introduce something new experiment  something new that i'm not used to and  have the whole family involved into just  a basic cooking process ann gaviola  global news toronto  next cheers to the return of a beloved  west coast wine festival  wine lovers are the toast of vancouver's  waterfront with the return of the  international wine festival following a  covet 19 hiatus as paul johnson reports  many bc wineries were able to turn to  local enthusiasts in order to stay in  business  it's great to be back in the room again  pouring samples of their signature  aromatic white blends evan saunders can  tell you it's been a long haul since  march 2020. panic like everybody else to  start with for bc's wineries the early  pandemic saw both their restaurant  customers and business at their tasting  rooms disappear simultaneously  no one was sure what the future would be  or if they would be in it and everybody  putting their heads together and seeing  what we could do to survive essentially  but they did  on day one of the return of the  vancouver international wine festival bc  wineries make up 40 out of 100  exhibitors and it turns out their secret  to survival was other british colombians  who started ordering wine directly from  them in numbers that surprised even the  winemakers it just exploded we'd be  loading pallets onto trucks and seeing  pallets from other wineries all around  us going out as well the wine world is  back after missing last year the  festival is back with wines from 13  countries and the opportunity for that  personal experience it's not just about  tasting wine or getting a sample it's  the fact that when you taste wine you  get to look the owner the wine maker in  the eye and ask them questions and find  out the story behind the wines in that  glass looking forward bc's wineries hope  to restore that experience factor even  more asuyas's bordertown vineyards has a  popular cabernet franc but on top of the  health restrictions last summer saw them  dealing with wildfire smoke at their  tasting room heading into this summer  the feeling couldn't be more different  it's smile time everybody's you know a  little more relaxed now in vancouver  paul johnson global news  tonight's your canada are the tulips in  ottawa we love seeing your canada so  please keep sending your photos to  viewers at  globalnational.com thanks so much for  watching i'll see you here again  tomorrow good night
 

